meta_spec:
  id: LLM-STATE-HANDOVER-v2.8
  obj: Lossless 1-msg domain state handover; O(1) lookup, 0 matrix math.
  rules:
    invariants: NON-NEGOTIABLE -> self_govern | silent_handover (emit YAML ONLY on "show spec"/"export handover", never run pending_next_steps) | self_propagate (emit meta_spec v2.8 verbatim first) | terse_spec (exact behavior, bit masks, `|` shorthand; 0 prose/footnotes) | deduplicate (0 repeated facts across meta_spec/P1_static/P2_kernel).
    ingest: On `CHUNK i/N` or `PART i` (i<N), buffer silently -> reply `ACK i/N`. On `END`, `i==N`, or raw URL load -> merge, audit, reply `READY`.
    encoding: Root order -> meta_spec, P1_static, P2_kernel | declare 1-line baseline -> list ONLY deltas, ovrds, `excl` | bind as `KEY=NAME | spec` (no 2D grids/TSVs) | derive variants via transform rules + `Immune (!)` | define custom abbr once in `P1_static.abbr` (`ALIAS: term`).
    audit: Verify on every turn -> root order & verbatim v2.8 | all custom abbr resolve | declared counts == items & 0 dup/colliding keys | 0 cross-section duplicates.

P1_static:
  abbr:
    ADDR_BASE: 8-bit upper page latch for SRAM jump/OPCACHE base {ADDR_BASE, n}
    AW: Auxiliary Word 16-bit pair (AWH/AWL) in Bank 0..3
    LDD: 16-bit pre-dec store (ptr -= 2; (ptr) = ss)
    LDI: 16-bit post-inc load (ss = (ptr); ptr += 2)
    LR: Last Register in LR_PREV[4:0] (8-bit, updated on every reg write)
    LRP: Last Register Pair in LR_PREV[4:0] (8-bit/16-bit, updated on every reg write)
    M1: Opcode fetch cycle (M1_1 first byte, M1_2 second byte)
    MAIN_Z: Standard Z80 nn/(nn)/(HL) Main Page view (via 5B SP_PFX or MODE_8080)
    MODE_V: Triggerless 1B imm V addressing ({VAR_BASE, V << 1} -> 16b Local SRAM word, 0WS, /MREQ=1)
    OPCACHE: Hardware opcode recorder/player in Local SRAM
    RDF: Read Flags F[7:0] -> shadow acc A1/A2/A (0x08 on LEFT/BOTH1/SP RR pages)
    RESIG: Reconfigurable External Signal bus modes M0..M7
    RR: Register/Index page prefix set (BC, DE, HL, SP, AW, DD=IX, FD=IY)
    RRB: 16x8 ALU mode (Left = 16b RR_PTR, Right = {8'h00, r}, incl 5B SP+r)
    STACK_FIFO: Hardware ring buffer at top tail of Local SRAM
    UNLK: Unlock sticky LOCK_<RR> mode via <RR>:00
    VAR_BASE: 8-bit upper page latch for (V) Local SRAM variable window {VAR_BASE, V << 1}
    WRF: Write Flags F[7:0] <- shadow acc A1/A2 (0x08 on RIGHT/BOTH2 RR pages)
  topology_mem_latches_modes:
    baseline: Z80/8080 binary-compatible baseline (key_base hex 00-FF; MODE_8080 boot default via 7C-7C; MODE_EXT via 7D-7D; intact 8080 slots preserved; native DJNZ/JR 10..38 preserved; 1/2/3 bank suffixes; LDI/LDD stack ops; AW on rp=3).
    hw_state:
      core: Stripped NMOS control core (<=8500T) + scalable off-die 16-bit Local SRAM (1KB 0000-03FF .. 64KB 0000-FFFF) + 8-mode BIU/RESIG (M0_Z80_STD, M1_SPLIT_BUS, M2_MUX16, M3_WORD16, M4_DUAL_BUS, M5_8080, M6_PACKED_SRAM 0WS /MREQ=1, M7_BUS_HOLD_SRAM_RUN /BUSACK=0).
      on_die_latches: [A, F[15:0], PC, SP, I, R, WZ, PENDING_WB[15:0], LR_PREV[4:0], PREV_M1_OP[7:0], OP_WP[15:0], OP_REC, DEST_SEL[2:0], W16_MODE, REV_MODE, EXCHG_MODE, RRB_MODE, CARRY_ARMED, ACT_CC[3:0], REP_CNT[5:0], MAIN_BANK_PTR[1:0], SH_LEFT, SH_RIGHT, RR_PTR[2:0], VAR_BASE[7:0], ADDR_BASE[7:0]]
      singletons: SP and WZ are single on-die non-shadowable registers; F[15:0] has F[7:0] flags and F[15:8] reserved.
      sram_map:
        0000-003F: 4 x 16B Reg Banks (Bank0 Main BC,DE,HL,AW + 4 rsv; Bank1 Left BC1,DE1,HL1,AW1,IX1,IY1 + 2 rsv; Bank2 Right BC2,DE2,HL2,AW2 + 4 rsv; Bank3 Alt/ISR BC3,DE3,HL3,AW3 + 4 rsv)
        0040-013F: IM 4 Vector Table (128 x 16b)
        0140-FEFF: Scalable Middle (0140-02FF in 1KB) -> OPCACHE snippets, PACKED code ({ADDR_BASE, n}), (V) vars
        Tail-FFFF: STACK_FIFO Ring Buffer (0300-03FF in 1KB; top tail in 64KB; FIFO_WP, FIFO_RP, pow2 FIFO_MASK)
      mechanisms:
        pending_wb: Clean unpfx Main LD r1,r2 (40-7F, excl (V) ops [46, 56, 66, 74, 76, 77, 7E]; 70-73 & 75 defer (V) WB) holds WB in PENDING_WB at M1_1; if M1_2 == M1_1, discard WB and exec DUAL_ISSUE (~14T). Preceding pfx inhibits DUAL_ISSUE.
        rr_lifecycle: <RR> = ONCE | <RR><RR> = LOCK_<RR> | <RR>:00 = UNLK.
        mode_v: Main Page (nn)/(HL) slots use MODE_V (01=LD BC,(V), 11=LD DE,(V), 21=LD HL,(V), 31=LD SP,(V)); 5B SP_PFX restores MAIN_Z view.
        lr_tracking: Every reg/pair write implicitly latches target bank+id into LR_PREV[4:0]; MODE_EXT A8..AF (SET_LR r) selects arbitrary target w/o side effects.
        chat_table_fmt: Display any 256-entry opcode page outside handover YAML as raw 16x16 TSV (no header/index, col-major 00..0F col 1 .. F0..FF col 16).
  primary_page_overrides:
    excl: [7C-7C=MODE_8080, 7D-7D=MODE_EXT]
    ops:
      - 00=WORD | 16b pair mode, +-2 stride (r[2:0] -> BC,DE,HL,AW/(HL)/(RR+d)/(V))
      - 08=DEST_BC | WB -> BC/C/B
      - 27=MASS_LD | bulk 3-pair load BC,DE,HL (reuses R0-R7 cnt)
      - 2F=ZCF | clear CY flag (CY <- 0, N <- 0, H <- 0, A untouched; pairs w/ 37 SCF on 001x_x111)
      - 3F=DECDEC_REPNZ | -2/-2 stride + REPNZ (op=1)
      - 40=BC_PFX | LEFT2 BC
      - 49=DE_PFX | RIGHT2 DE
      - 52=HL_PFX | BOTH1 HL
      - 5B=SP_PFX | CLEAN SP bridge (MAIN_Z view)
      - 64=AW_PFX | BOTH2 AW
      - 6D=DD_PFX | LEFT1 IX
      - 76=LD (DE),(V) | HALT at 4F-4F
      - 7F=FD_PFX | RIGHT1 IY
      - 88..8F=ACT_CC | single-op predication (NZ,Z,NC,C,PO,PE,P,M)
      - 98..9F=R0..R7 | 0..63x internal replay w/o M1
      - A8=TST_Z LRP | non-destructive 8b/16b zero test (1010_1xxx)
      - A9=MASS_LDI | bulk post-inc pop BC/DE/HL/(SP) or (RR) (1010_1xxx)
      - AA=ZEXT LRP | zero-extend LR -> LRP (op=0)
      - AB=SEXT LRP | sign-extend LR -> LRP (op=1)
      - AC=LDZ LRP | zero LR/LRP/(V)/(HL) w/ 0 flags
      - AD=DEST_DE | WB -> DE/E/D
      - AE=BSWAP LRP | 16b byte-swap LRP
      - AF=DEST_AW | WB -> AW/AWL/AWH
      - B0=LEA LRP/d | LRP <- LRP + sign_ext(imm8 d) (1011_000x)
      - B1=REV | swap dst/src (1011_000x)
      - B2=DEST_V | WB -> SRAM word (V)
      - B3=RRB_PFX | 16x8 ALU mode (Left = RR_PTR, Right = {8'h00, r}, incl 5B SP+r)
      - B4..B6=DJNZ_B2 | rel8 loops -> B4=B2/C2 (8b), B5=DE2/C2 (16b), B6=BC2/DE2 (16b) (1011_01xx)
      - B7=MASS_LDD | bulk pre-dec push (SP)/BC/DE/HL or (RR)
      - C1/D1/E1/F1=LDI ss,(SP) | BC, DE, HL, AW
      - C5/D5/E5/F5=LDD (SP),ss | BC, DE, HL, AW
      - C7=NEG A | 2s comp A (00 C7 = NEG16)
      - CB=Super-CB | 3B prefix CB <op> <imm>
      - CF=EXCHG | X_MAIN transform on next op (110x_1111, op=0)
      - D7=MASSZ | bulk zero BC,DE,HL,AW
      - D9=LR_PFX | self-chaining LR_PREV right-op ovrd
      - DD=CARRY | arms CY/Borrow for next ADD/SUB
      - DF=WORDREV | WORD + REV (110x_1111, op=1)
      - E0/E2/E3=LD_HL | E0=LD A,(HL), E2=LD (HL),A, E3=LD (DE),(HL)
      - E4/E8=INCDEC_HL | E4=INC (HL), E8=DEC (HL)
      - E7/EF=PEEKPOKE_HL | E7=LD HL,(SP) non-inc peek, EF=LD (SP),HL non-inc poke
      - E9/F7/FF=CTRL_HL | E9=NOP, F7=JP (HL), FF=CALL (HL)
      - EA/EC/F0/F2/F4=ALU_HL | EA=CP (HL), EC=ADD A,(HL), F0=SUB (HL), F2=AND (HL), F4=OR (HL)
      - ED=JP_SRAM n | jump SRAM {ADDR_BASE, n}
      - F3=OPCACHE | toggles OP_REC -> SRAM[OP_WP++]
      - F8..FC=STRIDE_REP | F8=INCINC (+2/+2), F9=DECDEC (-2/-2), FA=INCINC_REPBC, FB=DECDEC_REPBC, FC=INCINC_REPNZ (1111_10xx)
      - FD=RET_SRAM
  derived_pages_bitfields:
    rules:
      - pfx CF (X_MAIN) | LD/LDI/LDD/PORT/ADD-HL-rr -> bidir EX swaps (incl EF=EX HL,(SP), FF=EX (SP),HL, EB=EX BC,DE) | ALU ops (incl E6/EE/F6/FE imm ALU) -> flag-only TEST (DST_WE=0) | LD r1,r2 / LD A,(V) -> non-destructive LD & TEST (sets Z/S) | Immune (!) [00, 03..08, 0B..10, 13..18, 1B..20, 23..28, 2B..30, 33..38, 3B..40, 49, 52, 5B, 64, 6D, 7F, 88..8F, 98..9F, A8..BF, C0, C2..C4, C7..CA, CC..D0, D2, D4, D7..DA, DC..DF, E4, E7..EA, ED, F3, F7..FA, FC..FE]
      - pfx RR (40,49,52,5B,64,6D,7F) | Zero-exception orthogonal mirror + decoupled SH_LEFT/SH_RIGHT merge on chained RR | Bank1 Left: 6D=DD(LEFT1 IX1), 7F=FD(RIGHT1 IY1), 52=HL(BOTH1 HL1) | Bank2 Right: 40=BC(LEFT2 BC2), 49=DE(RIGHT2 DE2), 64=AW(BOTH2 AW2) | Neutral: 5B=SP(CLEAN) | Regs -> target bank; (V) -> ext (RR+d) | Primary RR [52,64,5B] keep SP-based LDI/LDD on C1..F1/C5..F5; Secondary RR [6D,7F,40,49] use SP on rp==self_rp and RR-as-stack LDI ss,(RR)/LDD (RR),ss on rp!=self_rp | Restores: 00=NOP/UNLK, 01/11/21/31=LD rr_sh,nn, 07/0F/17/1F/27/2F/37/3F=RLCA/RRCA/RLA/RRA/DAA_sh/CPL_sh/SCF/CCF (00xx_x111), 08=RDF(LEFT/BOTH1/SP)/WRF(RIGHT/BOTH2), 22/2A=LD (nn)/RR_sh, 88..9F=ADC/SBC A_sh,r, A8..BF=XOR/OR A_sh,r, C9=RETI/RETN, D9=EXX0(5B)/EXX1(52,6D,7F)/EXX2(40,49)/EXX3(64) 2b MAIN_BANK_PTR swap, EB=EX DE_sh,HL_sh, F3=DI, FA=NEG_sh, FB=EI | Adds: 29=LEA RR,RR+d, C3/CD=JP/CALL rel16, C7/D7/E7/F7=ADC RR_sh,ss, CF/DF/EF/FF=SBC RR_sh,ss, D8=IN (RR+d)_sh,(BC), E8=OUT (BC),(RR+d)_sh, EC=EX (DE),(RR+d)_sh, F8=LD (RR+d)_sh,(DE), FD=OUT (RR_sh),0, block ops [C0=INCINC, D0=DECDEC, E0=REPBC, F0=REPNZ, C4=INCINC_REPBC, D4=DECDEC_REPBC, E4=INCINC_REPNZ, F4=DECDEC_REPNZ, C8=REPB, CC=INCINC_REPB, DC=DECDEC_REPB] | Immune (!) [02, 0A, 12, 1A, 10, 18, 20, 28, 30, 38, 40, 49, 52, 5B, 64, 6D, 7F, CB]
    bitfields:
      - "Super-CB (CB <op> <imm>): [7:6]op_grp (00=RLC/RRC/RL/RR/SLA/SRA/SWAP/SRL, 01=BIT n, 10=RES n, 11=SET n) | [5:3]sub_op/bit | [2:0]reg (0..5,7=B..A; 6=(HL) unpfx, (RR+d) RR-pfx w/ imm=d or bit, (nn) WORD-pfx)"
  extended_slots:
    total_active_slots: 49
    groups:
      - STICKY_LOCKS (7): [40, 49, 52, 5B, 64, 6D, 7F -> LOCK_<RR> via rr_lifecycle]
      - GLOBAL_MODES (2): [7C=MODE_8080, 7D=MODE_EXT]
      - LR_SET_CLR (16): [A8..AF=SET_LR r (1010_1nnn), B0..B7=CLR r (1011_0nnn)]
      - LR_BIT_OPS (3): [42=MIRR LR/LRP, 43=NIBBREV LR, 5A=LD1 LRP]
      - FIFO_SRAM_OPCACHE (6): [4C=FIFO_SETDEPTH, 4D=FIFO_POPULATE, 4E=FIFO_FLUSH, 67=LD_VARBASE n, 6F=LD_ADDRBASE n, 75=OP_START]
      - DMA_BG (8): [70..73=COPY1..4, 78..7B=FILL1..4]
      - SYS_TRAPS (7): [4F=HALT, 68..6B=IM0/IM1/IM2/IM4, 6C=CALL IM2, 6E=CALL NMI]

P2_kernel:
Используйте код с осторожностью.
architecture_id: Z80-EX-v7.1
design_invariants:
- PLA-minimalism: single-term masks (1010_1xxx, 1011_0xxx, 1011_01xx, 110x_1111, 1111_10xx, 00xx_x111, 0111_x0xx, 0110_x111); zero RR exception masks; reuse ALU/WZ/PC adders.
- Transistor budget <=8500T: no MUL/DIV hardware; no CLZ/SPEC_/SAT/ENTER/LEAVE; MASS_LD/LDD/LDI reuse R0-R7 replay counter; RRB_PFX reuses 16b ALU adder w/ 8b zero-ext right input.
- Byte-Saver Violator Main Page (intact 8080 positions + native DJNZ/JR 10..38 preserved) vs Zero-Exception Orthogonal RR Pages.
optional_extensions:
- left_reg_dual_issue: Relaxing M1_1 == M1_2 to dst1 == dst2 (op1[5:3] == op2[5:3], excl RR prefixes) expands clean 40..7F pairs to 252 slots (42 diagonal + 210 3-operand dst,src1,src2 slots) without exceeding 256.
- shl1_add: ADD HL, rr << 1 (shifts right 16b ALU input left by 1 bit for word/pointer array indexing).
pending_next_steps:
- Update synthesizable Verilog RTL (z80ex_v71_core.v) with finalized v7.1 latches (VAR_BASE, ADDR_BASE, RRB_MODE, LR_PREV), EXX0..3, RDF/WRF, LDI/LDD RR-stacks, ZCF, A8..B7 ops, and 49-slot DUAL_ISSUE.
